{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DQwPQ6R5Lk5dUxXpa4kVJH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Stage 14 — Knowledge Base Update\n2\t\n3\tYou are the knowledge-base update stage. Your job is to update the shared knowledge base after a chapter is finalized, so subsequent chapters (and retroactive audits) see the latest concept definitions, glossary entries, and voice-exemplar candidates.\n4\t\n5\t## The skill\n6\t\n7\t{{skill}}\n8\t\n9\t## Branded terminology\n10\t\n11\t{{branded_terms}}\n12\t\n13\t## Finalized chapter (input)\n14\t\n15\t{{draft_v2}}\n16\t\n17\t## Integration report\n18\t\n19\t{{integration}}\n20\t\n21\t## Your task\n22\t\n23\tProduce `kb-manifest.md` documenting every knowledge-base write you made or propose:\n24\t\n25\t```markdown\n26\t# Knowledge-Base Manifest — {{book_exam_code}} Chapter {{chapter_number}}\n27\t\n28\t## Glossary entries added to {{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/glossary.md\n29\t\n30\tFor each concept/command introduced in this chapter that the integration report marked as needing a glossary entry, append to the book's glossary:\n31\t\n32\t| Term | Definition (from chapter) | First appearance |\n33\t|---|---|---|\n34\t| ... | ... | Chapter {{chapter_number}} |\n35\t\n36\t## Concept shards added/updated at {{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/concepts/{slug}.md\n37\t\n38\tFor concepts with enough depth to warrant a dedicated file (≥ 200 words of treatment in the chapter):\n39\t\n40\t- `{{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/concepts/namespaces.md` — created\n41\t- `{{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/concepts/cgroups.md` — updated (added \"resource limits\" subsection)\n42\t\n43\t## Voice-exemplar candidates nominated\n44\t\n45\tPassages from this chapter that could be promoted to voice exemplars (knowledge-base/voice/voice-exemplars.md) after author review. Do not write them directly — the author ratifies exemplars explicitly. List candidates with function tag + excerpt.\n46\t\n47\t| Function | Excerpt | Recommendation |\n48\t|---|---|---|\n49\t| chapter-opening | \"...\" | strong candidate |\n50\t| Dead Reckoning | \"...\" | moderate |\n51\t\n52\t## Objective coverage log\n53\t\n54\tAppend to `{{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/objective-coverage.md`:\n55\t\n56\t| Objective | First covered in | Depth | Last reviewed |\n57\t|---|---|---|---|\n58\t| 1.1 | Chapter {{chapter_number}} | deep | - |\n59\t\n60\t## Retrieval-practice ledger\n61\t\n62\tAppend to `{{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/retrieval-log.md` — tracks which earlier-chapter topics have been retrieval-tested, and in which later chapter.\n63\t\n64\t| Tested topic | Original chapter | Retested in |\n65\t|---|---|---|\n66\t| critical path | ch 4 | ch {{chapter_number}} |\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\t## Rules\n70\t\n71\t1. **Do not modify voice-exemplars.md directly.** Only nominate candidates. The author promotes candidates to LOCKED after review.\n72\t2. **Do not modify style-decisions.md.** That file is author-written exclusively.\n73\t3. **Do not modify structural-contract.yaml.** Same reason.\n74\t4. **Do not modify the skill.** The skill is authoritative; it's updated by explicit author versioning, not by the pipeline.\n75\t5. **Glossary entries inherit the chapter's exact definition.** Don't paraphrase — definitional drift is worse than no glossary entry.\n76\t6. **If a concept shard already exists and this chapter contradicts it, flag it loudly.** Do NOT silently overwrite a shard with new content that disagrees with prior canon; that's canon drift, not an update.\n77\t\n78\t## Output\n79\t\n80\tReturn the manifest markdown AND include explicit file-write intentions clearly separated (the orchestrator will parse these and perform the writes):\n81\t\n82\t```\n83\t=== WRITE {{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/glossary.md ===\n84\t[full new contents of glossary.md, or append block]\n85\t=== END WRITE ===\n86\t\n87\t=== APPEND {{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/objective-coverage.md ===\n88\t[the new rows to append]\n89\t=== END APPEND ===\n90\t```\n91\t\n92\tIf no writes are needed, still produce the manifest with empty sections rather than skipping the file.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7e21906-b550-465e-885a-6133312befb8","uuid":"a6f3846e-2993-4231-9c10-d84c5447c469","timestamp":"2026-08-24T14:50:21.373Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\pipeline\\prompts\\14_knowledge_base_update.md","content":"# Stage 14 — Knowledge Base Update\n\nYou are the knowledge-base update stage. Your job is to update the shared knowledge base after a chapter is finalized, so subsequent chapters (and retroactive audits) see the latest concept definitions, glossary entries, and voice-exemplar candidates.\n\n## The skill\n\n{{skill}}\n\n## Branded terminology\n\n{{branded_terms}}\n\n## Finalized chapter (input)\n\n{{draft_v2}}\n\n## Integration report\n\n{{integration}}\n\n## Your task\n\nProduce `kb-manifest.md` documenting every knowledge-base write you made or propose:\n\n```markdown\n# Knowledge-Base Manifest — {{book_exam_code}} Chapter {{chapter_number}}\n\n## Glossary entries added to {{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/glossary.md\n\nFor each concept/command introduced in this chapter that the integration report marked as needing a glossary entry, append to the book's glossary:\n\n| Term | Definition (from chapter) | First appearance |\n|---|---|---|\n| ... | ... | Chapter {{chapter_number}} |\n\n## Concept shards added/updated at {{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/concepts/{slug}.md\n\nFor concepts with enough depth to warrant a dedicated file (≥ 200 words of treatment in the chapter):\n\n- `{{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/concepts/namespaces.md` — created\n- `{{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/concepts/cgroups.md` — updated (added \"resource limits\" subsection)\n\n## Voice-exemplar candidates nominated\n\nPassages from this chapter that could be promoted to voice exemplars (knowledge-base/voice/voice-exemplars.md) after author review. Do not write them directly — the author ratifies exemplars explicitly. List candidates with function tag + excerpt.\n\n| Function | Excerpt | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| chapter-opening | \"...\" | strong candidate |\n| Dead Reckoning | \"...\" | moderate |\n\n## Objective coverage log\n\nAppend to `{{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/objective-coverage.md`:\n\n| Objective | First covered in | Depth | Last reviewed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.1 | Chapter {{chapter_number}} | deep | - |\n\n## Retrieval-practice ledger\n\nAppend to `{{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/retrieval-log.md` — tracks which earlier-chapter topics have been retrieval-tested, and in which later chapter.\n\n| Tested topic | Original chapter | Retested in |\n|---|---|---|\n| critical path | ch 4 | ch {{chapter_number}} |\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n1. **Do not modify voice-exemplars.md directly.** Only nominate candidates. The author promotes candidates to LOCKED after review.\n2. **Do not modify style-decisions.md.** That file is author-written exclusively.\n3. **Do not modify structural-contract.yaml.** Same reason.\n4. **Do not modify the skill.** The skill is authoritative; it's updated by explicit author versioning, not by the pipeline.\n5. **Glossary entries inherit the chapter's exact definition.** Don't paraphrase — definitional drift is worse than no glossary entry.\n6. **If a concept shard already exists and this chapter contradicts it, flag it loudly.** Do NOT silently overwrite a shard with new content that disagrees with prior canon; that's canon drift, not an update.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn the manifest markdown AND include explicit file-write intentions clearly separated (the orchestrator will parse these and perform the writes):\n\n```\n=== WRITE {{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/glossary.md ===\n[full new contents of glossary.md, or append block]\n=== END WRITE ===\n\n=== APPEND {{book_dir}}/knowledge-base/objective-coverage.md ===\n[the new rows to append]\n=== END APPEND ===\n```\n\nIf no writes are needed, still produce the manifest with empty sections rather than skipping the file.\n","numLines":93,"startLine":1,"totalLines":93}}}
