{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01THHPGuj4dcKrFfFtx7VRPe","type":"tool_result","content":"15\t## Node status\n16\tA Node's status contains: Addresses (HostName, ExternalIP, InternalIP); Conditions; Capacity and Allocatable; Info (kernel version, container runtime, kubelet version). Conditions describe the status of all Running nodes: Ready — True if the node is healthy and ready to accept pods, False if the node is not healthy and is not accepting pods, and Unknown if the node controller has not heard from the node in the last node-monitor-grace-period; DiskPressure — True if pressure exists on the disk size; MemoryPressure — True if pressure exists on the node memory; PIDPressure — True if pressure exists on the processes; NetworkUnavailable — True if the network for the node is not correctly configured. `kubectl describe node <name>` shows them.\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7e21906-b550-465e-885a-6133312befb8","uuid":"ab76b027-238c-4570-979d-529b7308e2b7","timestamp":"2026-08-24T14:54:12.061Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\k8s-docs-nodes-2026-08-23.md","content":"## Node status\nA Node's status contains: Addresses (HostName, ExternalIP, InternalIP); Conditions; Capacity and Allocatable; Info (kernel version, container runtime, kubelet version). Conditions describe the status of all Running nodes: Ready — True if the node is healthy and ready to accept pods, False if the node is not healthy and is not accepting pods, and Unknown if the node controller has not heard from the node in the last node-monitor-grace-period; DiskPressure — True if pressure exists on the disk size; MemoryPressure — True if pressure exists on the node memory; PIDPressure — True if pressure exists on the processes; NetworkUnavailable — True if the network for the node is not correctly configured. `kubectl describe node <name>` shows them.\n","numLines":3,"startLine":15,"totalLines":23}}}
